<http://data.silknow.org/object/defe85a2-0b5c-39e1-8203-226c146f2e10/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Bed curtain, embroidered in red blue green and white silk on linen, in darning, satin and chain stitches. Up each side are vertical bands each with three vertical rows of alternating 'King' and 'Queen' patterns (Wace's designation for the patterns derived from pair of leaves surmounted by birds, trees and/or miniature flowers). The gable has King and Queen pattern, birds and animals. At the bottom are three horizontal rows of King and Queen pattern. These motifs are described as broad leaf (platyphyllenio) and branch (spitha) motifs in the Benaki Museum catalogue.\nThe front opening has been sewn up."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/defe85a2-0b5c-39e1-8203-226c146f2e10> .

